# Source-distribution contents.
#
# package-dir = {enhanced_agent_bus = "."} makes the repository root the package
# directory, so the top-level tests/ tree lands in the sdist. Measured from a clean
# checkout before this file existed: 1522 members, 3.4 MB, 513 of them test files.
# The explicit `[tool.setuptools] packages` list in pyproject.toml keeps tests out
# of the *wheel* and says nothing about the sdist, which is why both exist.
#
# Only the top-level tests/ needs pruning. The per-package tests directories
# (api/tests, observability/tests, ...) are not listed packages, so setuptools
# never collects them — `prune api/tests` and friends are no-ops. Measured, not
# assumed: removing them changes the archive by zero members. Do not add them back.

prune tests

# Working-copy hygiene. A clean checkout has none of these, so they are no-ops in
# CI; they exist so an sdist built in a developer tree matches the one CI builds
# instead of shipping whatever local build/ and __pycache__ happen to hold.
prune build
prune dist
prune htmlcov
prune node_modules
prune .venv
prune venv
global-exclude *.py[cod]
global-exclude __pycache__/*
